From 8ce1d3593519fb3e95fe8c960474c8dd9d8411dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:20:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Verify source signatures with openpgpverify

Replace the GnuPG-based %gpgverify with %openpgpverify, which uses
Sequoia sqv and takes the same options, as part of the Fedora 45 Change
https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Sequoia_openpgpverify

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 fcitx5-unikey.spec | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fcitx5-unikey.spec b/fcitx5-unikey.spec
index bb71ed0..d079e59 100644
--- a/fcitx5-unikey.spec
+++ b/fcitx5-unikey.spec
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ Source1:    https://download.fcitx-im.org/fcitx5/%{name}/%{name}-%{version}.tar.
 #   sq --home=none network keyserver search 2CC8A0609AD2A479C65B6D5C8E8B898CBF2412F9 --output 0x8E8B898CBF2412F9 --overwrite
 Source2:    https://pgp.key-server.io/download/0x8E8B898CBF2412F9
 
-BuildRequires:  gnupg2
+BuildRequires:  openpgpverify
 BuildRequires:  cmake
 BuildRequires:  extra-cmake-modules
 BuildRequires:  gcc-c++
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ Requires:       fcitx5-data
 Unikey (Vietnamese Input Method) engine support for Fcitx5.
 
 %prep
-%{gpgverify} --keyring='%{SOURCE2}' --signature='%{SOURCE1}' --data='%{SOURCE0}'
+%{openpgpverify} --keyring='%{SOURCE2}' --signature='%{SOURCE1}' --data='%{SOURCE0}'
 %autosetup
 
 %build
-- 
2.56.0

